  "rule": "Preserve clocks 90, contact gates from command one, the 72-command amplitude ramp, cap 0.5994550408719347, swing-end recontact timing, actual position references and smooth lift. Select V38's pose-separated wave velocity with an explicit previous-wave memory; initialization and amplitude activation/deactivation add zero rate. Keep all joint, speed and force bounds and physical timing unchanged.",
  "parameter_basis": "V36's 163 held landing commands have reachable, joint-limit-valid goals while measured joints lag their references. The old motor law is reconstructed for 3200 commands. V37 adds reference-rate tracking using coefficient 1 + existing damping, not outcome-fitted gains. Its native component preserves all 400 same-input position paths and gate memories; speed-cap use rises from 0 to 280 commands. Neither arithmetic nor reachability predicts a successful native trajectory.",
